    "description": "Construct new driveway approach of 18 FT.\n\nI have begun reviewing your application request. For more information on our permit requirements visit: https://www.austintexas.gov/transportation-public-works/right-way-row-permits\nThe items below MUST be provided before review can continue. Reply to this email once you have uploaded all required items to the ABC Portal. A response must be provided within 30 days or your request may be rejected due to inactivity. Additional comments may apply once the above has been confirmed.  \n\nPlan\nPlease provide a plan highlighting the sidewalk work scope. \n\nTraffic Control Plan\nThe permit was issued with 804S2-Sheet 2. This will not work with in the 100 FT of the intersection. I can let you know more once you provide the plan.\n\nAdditional comments may apply once the above has been confirmed.  \n\n8/12/26\n\nGood afternoon\n\n1.\tLet me know what Sam says if he ask you to add the sidewalk I can do form my end.\n2.\tThe permit was issued with 804 S2-Sheet which for a lane closure you can not use it with in the 100 ft of the intersection. only if-\na.\tthis closure is required to stage work equipments/ park work vehicle.\nb.\tIf you can have the closure 100 ft away from the intersection.\nc.\tYou can not close the alley entries.\n3.\tOther recommendations are Standard Detail 804S-4 sheet 3 (top half) behind the curb closure ONLY; staging from private property  and Special details 4 way flagger details. Let me know you thorughts.\n\nSidewalk Condition\nThis work will require a sidewalk closure. The standard 804S-1 sheet 4 (sidewalk closure) would NOT work because the detour route would be greater than 660 feet. Instead we could list a condition on our permit that you would be able to provide ADA accessibility the entire time. The condition would look like this Contractor MUST have crew present to halt work activities and escort pedestrians through or around the work area. Crew shall not impede travel lanes crosswalks alleyways fire hydrants or local access to all property. Please confirm this would be possible.",
